AI-generated articles fail JSON parsing due to double quotes in HTML attributes, and article content renders without proper heading/list/table styling.

## Changes

### JSON Parse Fix (`server.js`)
- Updated AI system prompt to explicitly require single quotes for HTML attributes
- Added response preview logging on parse failure for debugging

```javascript
// Before: AI uses double quotes breaking JSON
"htmlContent": "<p class=\"mb-4\">..."  // Parse error

// After: Single quotes instruction
KRITISCH VOOR JSON: Gebruik in HTML ALLEEN enkele quotes (')
```

### Article Styling (`AdminPanel.tsx`, `App.tsx`)
- Replaced Tailwind prose classes with explicit `.article-preview` CSS
- Covers H1-H3 hierarchy, lists, blockquotes, tables, figures with consistent dark theme styling

```css
.article-preview h1 { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; color: white; }
.article-preview h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #1e40af; }
.article-preview blockquote { border-left: 4px solid #3b82f6; background: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.1); }
```

### Already Present
- `created_at: new Date().toISOString()` verified in all article save paths (lines 558, 572, 623)

